WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.259
When it comes to acting on prestige TV, how
did the year fare in terms of its highest

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.940
highs and lowest lows?

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.100
We're here to explore just that.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:15.360
These are the best and worst TV performances
of 2019, from the pint-sized zombie slayers

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.040
to the post-apocalyptic tribal leaders.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.400
GLOW has always loved the seamier side of
the entertainment industry.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.880
Taking the cast to Las Vegas in the latest
season was a natural evolution of that.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.420
Characters like Sheila, rooted in artifice,
were forced to strip down, while practical

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.990
types like Ruth discovered the joy of glitz.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:38.140
Debbie, the show's headlining Liberty Belle,
did a little bit of both while falling for

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.310
a charismatic businessman, struggling with
the realities of motherhood, and becoming

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.760
a true producer.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.740
Betty Gilpin has always been one of the show's
most impressive assets.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.530
But in offering Debbie what seemed to be a
ticket to easy street, GLOW allowed Gilpin

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:56.080
to take the character to an entirely new plane
of characterization.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.200
This means portraying Debbie with a forthright
unpleasantness, but never losing the character's

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.460
steely, battle-tested resolve.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:08.200
Gilpin dares the viewer to judge Debbie for
throwing up cheeseburgers and double-crossing

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.090
lovers, and forces them to admit the reality
of her life.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.800
It's daring, and it pays off massively.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.620
In The Widow, Kate Beckinsale plays a woman
named Georgia who spots her allegedly dead

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.860
husband in a news broadcast from Kinshasa.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.900
It's immediately clear that Georgia desperately
wants to be the hard-bitten heroine of so

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.600
many action thrillers.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.440
She gets on a plane to the Congo immediately
upon spotting her husband's distinctive orange

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.560
hat and starts demanding answers once she
gets there.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.240
She's a take-no-prisoners kind of character.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:45.140
Unfortunately, that kind of performance demands
nuance, and Beckinsale does not provide that

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:45.780
nuance.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.320
"It's all we've got.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:48.560
We have to try."

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.020
"Okay, okay.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.480
I will collect you in the morning."

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.560
"Appreciate it."

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:59.120
The central mystery at the heart of the story
is juicy enough to carry a show forward, but

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.240
Beckinsale herself doesn't inspire much sympathy.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:08.140
Add in the saintly excesses of later episodes,
in which Georgia saves a child soldier, and

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.999
you get a character plagued by the worst of
two worlds: the irritatingly selfish foreigner

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.200
and the absurdly selfless savior.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.200
The result is a mishmash of tropes that no
one in their right mind would bother to root

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:19.720
for.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:25.080
Despite the controversy of Game of Thrones'
final season, there is one thing everyone

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:29.129
can agree on: Lyanna Mormont stole every scene
she was in.

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:34.559
Bella Ramsey plays the pint-sized Lady of
Bear Island with an intensity that goes beyond

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.500
charming all the way into genuinely heart-wrenching.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:44.560
"You left Winterfell a king and came back
a…I'm not sure what you are now."

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.080
Sure, it's cute to see the girl talking tougher
than all the grizzled men of the North, but

00:02:49.099 --> 00:02:53.870
her death at the hands of an undead giant
is one of the most tragic moments of the entire

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.160
last season.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:03:00.739
Lyanna is the spirit of the North incarnate,
a child forced to grow up by circumstances

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:02.159
beyond her control.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.540
Yet, in her unwavering commitment to honor,
she's a figure of ironclad inspiration.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.560
Ramsey forces the audience to take her as
seriously and courageously as she does her

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.420
countrymen.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:18.060
She doesn't live to see the triumph of life
over death, but she had as much a hand in

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.320
it as all the other headlining names of Game
of Thrones.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:26.859
Ramsey plays the character with such verve,
passion, and bravery, and no fan is likely

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:27.860
to forget that.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.279
Game of Thrones was as known for its villains
as its heroes.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.280
Joffrey, the surpassingly cruel boy-king,
was a monster without peer.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.859
Ramsay Bolton terrorized the North for years.

00:03:40.859 --> 00:03:45.599
Cersei, despite having a bit more nuance to
her nastiness, became one of the worst people

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.760
in Westeros through sheer spite.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.080
Westeros might have been a place of lords
and ladies, but audiences loved it for the

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.280
darkness underneath all that glamor.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:59.760
Euron Greyjoy is Thrones' last attempt at
a true monster, clearly built to fill the

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.589
void after Ramsay's death.

00:04:01.589 --> 00:04:06.589
He sneers, postures, and makes lewd jokes
with the sort of swagger that made his predecessors

00:04:06.589 --> 00:04:07.780
so hate-worthy.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.420
But that's all he ever amounts to, a worn-out
copy of better characters.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:17.960
He's more annoying than dangerous, a buzzing
fly rather than a stalking beast.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.180
When he dies, there's no catharsis.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.880
It's more of a relief than anything else to
know that he won't be wasting anymore screen

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:24.580
time.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:29.180
Greyjoy might've considered himself the man
who finally killed Jaime Lannister, but in

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:34.460
truth, he was only ever an irritating, unworthy
distraction in an already overstuffed show.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.420
Midge Maisel of The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel
could've been insufferable.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:45.060
A wealthy, mid-century woman of New York City,
she has an enormous apartment, flawless hair,

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.021
and a family servant who takes care of everyday
tasks like cooking, grocery shopping, and

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.021
child-raising.

00:04:50.021 --> 00:04:56.390
Midge has it all, remaining, even in the face
of her crumbling marriage, unstoppably competent,

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:59.060
chipper, and immaculately styled.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:05.240
But Rachel Brosnahan never lets the viewer
forget one crucial fact: Midge knows exactly

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:10.140
how good she is at what she does and exactly
what being that person requires.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:15.560
Her charm, talent, and poise are all the result
of tireless work, whether that takes the form

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.760
of exhaustive beauty routines or a crammed
comedienne's notebook.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:24.980
Brosnahan plays Midge as a woman who's justifiably
proud of her accomplishments, but never without

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:28.120
the wry knowledge of how hard the world makes
her work for them.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:32.980
Moreover, for as sarcastic a character as
Midge can be, Brosnahan infuses her with an

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.160
immense warmth and generosity.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:38.840
She might crack a joke here and there about
her friends, but she never stops wanting to

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:40.880
make their lives richer and happier.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:45.760
Brosnahan's eyes glitter with ambition when
Midge faces an obstacle, and it's a delight

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.520
to watch.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.740
Pete Davidson certainly seems to believe he's
funny.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.820
Audiences know this because he's apparently
unable to get through his performances without

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:54.640
joking.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:59.540
Every SNL sketch he's featured in seems to
contain at least one moment in which he breaks

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.420
into giggles.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.280
Perhaps Davidson believes this is charming,
even adding to the humor.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.400
For the rest of us, it's tiresome.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.960
"I mean, what is this?"

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:08.620
"Your kitchen!"

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.320
"No, I mean, us.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.820
I really hope you understand, but we have
to end this."

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:14.500
"Okay."

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:15.720
Think for a second.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.740
What comes to mind when the words "Pete Davidson"
are said?

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:23.820
Probably his broken engagement with Ariana
Grande, perhaps a few of his off-color remarks.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:28.720
Only then does one remember he is, technically,
a comedian and a regular player on Saturday

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:29.730
Night Live.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:33.260
He struggles through his lines like a high
schooler who thinks he really might have a

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.980
shot at this whole improv thing.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:39.620
His effort is audible in both his breaks into
laughter and the generally strained way he

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.160
delivers his comedy.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:46.520
He's best as the dopey stoner type, but he's
made quite clear that that's pretty much who

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.500
he is anyway.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:52.760
He's barely a comedian and certainly not an
actor, two qualities that are required for

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.160
SNL to do what it does.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.720
He is merely Pete Davidson.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:59.940
And to everyone who isn't terribly interested
in what that means for him off-screen, that's

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.700
not nearly enough to justify his spot in the
cast.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:07.780
The Good Place pulls off a truly devilish
double-act with its premise.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.460
It's all about the exploits of people condemned
to an afterlife in "the bad place" who just

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.080
can't quit trying to do better.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:19.920
The cast's obvious talent is key to its success,
but even among such standout performers, Ted

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.960
Danson manages to impress.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:27.660
As Michael, an immortal architect of their
afterlife, he's both devil and angel, punisher

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:28.800
and victim.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.780
Does he have an endearing affection for the
mundane-ness of human life?

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:33.780
Absolutely.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:38.420
Does he also spend his endless days devising
new and better ways to torture humans for

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.200
eternity?

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.420
Well, yes.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.900
But he also loves humanity's many oddities.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:46.460
"I put a coin in a thing and got a gumball!

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:50.780
And then someone came up to me and said, 'Hot
enough for ya?' and you know what I said?

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.580
I said, 'tell me about it!'"

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:54.220
Danson's genius is in his delicacy.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:59.080
Michael never falls into adorable quirkiness,
nor does his growing appreciation of ethics

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.800
threaten his truly alien characteristics.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:07.020
He's as unknowable as a character that generally
appears to be human can be, and his storyline

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.440
is a careful reveal over the course of many
episodes.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:13.540
It's a balancing act that few actors could
pull off.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:18.800
Yet Danson makes Michael's wide-eyed innocence
as convincing as his total ignorance of basic

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:19.580
decency.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:25.120
He might be a billion-year-old fire squid
wearing a humanoid skin, but you can't help

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.580
but root for him anyway.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:33.000
What do you get if you put the dystopias of
YA fiction, Game of Thrones, and every high-profile

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.300
narrative video game of the past decade into
a blender?

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:40.960
The answer is See, and it's just as discordant
as that description implies.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:46.220
Set in a post-apocalyptic world in which nearly
everyone has lost their sight, Jason Momoa

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:50.240
plays Baba Voss, whose newborn twins have
the ability to see.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:55.519
Naturally, they are coveted by bad guys, and
Voss must journey across a threatening landscape

00:08:55.519 --> 00:08:56.660
to protect them.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:09:00.689
Fight scenes, love scenes, and everything
else you desperately need to be crowned the

00:09:00.689 --> 00:09:04.520
successor to Game of Thrones ensue, with no
expense spared.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.700
See certainly looks good.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:09.980
Unfortunately, that's about all it succeeds
at.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:14.540
There are many to blame for this, but Momoa
is certainly the most visible.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:19.800
Voss is stoic, good at fighting, and generally
cool, but that's pretty much where his character

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:20.580
ends.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:26.540
Voss feels assembled in a lab, a warrior dude
who might've headlined any action franchise.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:31.379
That blandness doesn't save him, but damns
him to second-tier status forever behind the

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.240
characters that inspired him.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:38.660
Baba Voss tries desperately to be cool, and
as anyone can tell you, visible effort will

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:41.000
keep one from coolness forever.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:46.640
Hulu's dramatization of Gypsy Rose and Dee
Dee Blanchard's complex dance of cruelty,

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.140
appeasement, and ultimately, murder, could've
collapsed in a pile of melodrama.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:54.280
It's a testament to the skill of its cast
that it didn't.

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:59.110
A big part of that credit belongs to Joey
King, who portrays Gypsy as a survivor against

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.200
all odds.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:05.700
Viewers likely entered The Act knowing its
ending, but King's delicacy makes every inevitable

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.660
moment an edge-of-the-seat event.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.860
Watching Gypsy's good-girl demeanor crumble
is a revelation, one that's as surprising

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:14.960
to Gypsy as it is to her mother.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:19.120
When Gypsy realizes she might not be deathly
allergic to sugar as her mother has always

00:10:19.129 --> 00:10:24.579
told her, betrayal and hope flash across her
face, then are buried, swiftly, to maintain

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:25.460
the peace.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:29.980
But the seed has been planted, and watching
it flower within Gypsy is a performance worth

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:30.980
anyone's time.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:36.600
Over the course of eight episodes, King develops
the character from an abused girl to a premeditated

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.460
killer.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:43.000
Yet King never lets the audience forget that
whatever mask Gypsy wears, it's only one of

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:43.760
many.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:49.059
King plays a consummate actress in The Act,
and in so doing, establishes herself as one

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:51.620
of Hollywood's most intriguing new talents.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:56.020
The CW wants you to know that this is not
your mother's Nancy Drew.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:11:01.300
In this iteration of the teen detective's
adventures, there's romance, murder, and occult

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:06.240
intrigue, everything that made sister show
Riverdale the success it's become.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.620
Who doesn't love a bit of garish, soapy fun
once in a while?

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:14.800
A good cast can turn such a premise into a
true success, potentially even erasing the

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.920
"guilty" in "guilty pleasure," especially
when it comes to teen drama.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:23.760
After all, if it can work for the sunshiny
denizens of Archie Comics, why couldn't it

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.260
work for Nancy Drew?

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:31.480
In execution, however, this wasn't the case,
and lead actress Kennedy McMann is an enormous

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:32.620
part of why.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:38.140
This Nancy has it considerably less together
than her literary self, still reeling from

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:41.820
the death of her mother and the disastrous
senior year that entailed.

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:47.400
This is an intriguing take on the character,
but it only really results in a dreary performance

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:50.730
that leaves one longing for the can-do spirit
of the original.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:56.459
Sure, painting her mystery-solving as more
of a compulsion than a calling is a neat idea,

00:11:56.459 --> 00:12:00.939
but that sort of rewrite necessitates an actress
who can sell the contrast between the original

00:12:00.939 --> 00:12:03.670
heroine and the TV show's struggling girl.

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:08.339
McMann, whose acting is mostly confined to
her eyebrows, is not that heroine, resulting

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:11.300
in one of the worst TV performances of 2019.

